course: dictionary
lesson: 13521
title: Words that warn of what is coming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Impending is a describing word, an adjective. It means about to happen soon, and it is often something unpleasant or important. «The dark clouds were a sign of an impending storm.» The storm has not arrived yet, but it is very close.
explain: The words around impending give you clues. Dark clouds, a warning, or a long wait all show that something is near. «The villagers locked their doors, sensing impending danger.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? Something coming soon, and probably bad. Then swap in your meaning, "sensing danger about to happen soon", and check it still makes sense.
explain: Impending does not mean far away. It means close at hand. «Mum cleaned the whole house for the impending visit of Grandma.» Grandma is not in the house yet, but her visit is coming soon, so the cleaning has begun.
fact: Impending means about to happen soon.
fact: Impending is often used for something unpleasant or important, such as danger, a storm or a test.
fact: «Impending doom» means a terrible fate that seems about to happen, and writers use it to build suspense in stories.
fact: In news and weather, impending describes events close at hand, such as «an impending storm».
fact: A good check is to swap in "about to happen soon" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Dark clouds gathered, warning of an impending storm.» What does impending mean? | *About to happen soon | Very colourful | Long gone and over | Quiet and calm
exercise: «The class felt a thrill at the impending school trip.» What does impending suggest? | *Coming very soon | Happened last week | Hidden under a bed | Far away in the past
exercise: «Wolves howled, and the villagers felt impending danger.» Find and copy the word that means about to happen soon. | *impending | howled | villagers | felt
test: «The hikers hurried home before the impending rain.» What does impending mean here? | Moving very fast | Long over and forgotten | Pretty and colourful | *About to happen soon
test: Which phrase best matches "impending doom"? | *A terrible fate that is about to happen | A happy party from last year | A long nap after lunch | A quiet walk in the park
exam: Ella reads «an impending visit from Grandma». Which meaning fits best? | *Coming soon | Painted red | Very loud | Gone for ever
